  "notes": [
    "Partial encoding of Alaska Medicaid Inhaled Prostacycline Mimetic Criteria, Version 1; Original 12/2/2021; Approval 1/21/22; Effective 2022-03-01. Products: Tyvaso (treprostinil inhaled) and Ventavis (iloprost).",
    "Encoded shared Group 1 PAH and Tyvaso-only Group 3 PH-ILD approval paths. FDA labeled age for PAH is an attestation; PH-ILD requires age ≥18. RHC pressure/resistance bands preserve every source threshold, including strict PVR >3 and the 6.25 WU branch boundary.",
    "Denial criterion: failure to meet approval criteria only. No additive clinical denials. Class II steps require trial and failure or contraindication; no minimum trial duration or intolerance exception is specified.",
    "Cautions (notes only): symptomatic hypotension, including increased hypotensive effects of vasodilators and antihypertensives; increased bleeding risk, particularly with anticoagulants.",
    "Duration (notes only): initial approval up to 3 months; reauthorization up to 12 months with documented improvement or stability from baseline in 6-minute walk distance, OR improved or stable functional class if the walk test is inappropriate.",
    "Quantity (notes only): 34-day supply. max_units is null; quantity is not evaluated.",
    "Documentation verification, cautions, duration, reauthorization and quantity require manual review; this pack remains partial."
  ],
